;; tests/clojure-suite/ORACLE-ASSERTIONS.edn
;;
;; ============================================================
;; THIS FILE IS THE DENOMINATOR OF THIS PROJECT'S NORTH STAR METRIC.
;; ============================================================
;;
;; CONFORMANCE-GUARANTEE.md defines mova's headline compatibility number
;; as "the percentage of assertions in Clojure 1.13.0-alpha6's own
;; test/clojure/test_clojure/ suite that pass when run under mova". The
;; NUMERATOR (assertions mova actually passed) lives in
;; tests/clojure-suite/scoreboard.edn. The DENOMINATOR -- how many
;; assertions each vendored file actually contains, a fact about the
;; test file itself, independent of what mova currently does -- lives
;; HERE, and only here. Deriving the denominator from mova's own run
;; (as scoreboard.edn alone used to do) makes the headline number
;; NON-MONOTONE: fixing a bug that unblocks a file injects that file's
;; failing assertions into the denominator and the number can go DOWN
;; even though mova got strictly better. This file breaks that by being
;; a fixed, mova-independent ground truth.
;;
;; Regenerate with:      bash tools/oracle-census.sh
;; (needs the Clojure CLI + JDK 21 on PATH, network access the first
;; time to resolve org.clojure/test.check + org.clojure/test.generative
;; from Maven Central, and tools/bootstrap-oracle.sh's pinned real
;; Clojure 1.13.0-alpha6 oracle -- run tools/bootstrap-oracle.sh first
;; if .oracle/ does not exist yet. Takes several minutes: every one of
;; the ~48 vendored files is run TWICE, each time in its own fresh JVM
;; process, under a wall-clock timeout.)
;;
;; HOW THE NUMBERS ARE PRODUCED: each vendored file under
;; tests/clojure-suite/vendor/ is required and run via real
;; clojure.test/run-tests -- NOT mova, NOT the mova-test-shim, NOT a
;; grep over `(is ...)`/`(are ...)` text (grepping badly undercounts:
;; `are` expands to N assertions per form, and `is` forms inside
;; loops/doseq execute many times each). clojure.test's own
;; *report-counters* after run-tests -- :pass + :fail + :error -- is
;; the executed-assertion count; :test is the deftest count. Real
;; Clojure's own pass/fail/error breakdown is recorded per file too:
;; if real Clojure itself fails or errors on an assertion, mova failing
;; it later is not mova's bug.
;;
;; The classpath (built by tools/oracle-census.sh) includes the pinned
;; upstream test/ tree so a file's own :requires of companion
;; namespaces resolve (e.g. protocols.clj's protocols/examples.clj
;; subdirectory companions), org.clojure/test.check and
;; org.clojure/test.generative at the exact versions the pinned
;; commit's own pom.xml declares, the suite's compiled Java test
;; fixtures (test/java/**), and a small fixed preamble
;; (clojure.test-helper, clojure.set, clojure.pprint -- see
;; tools/oracle-census.clj's own module doc for exactly why) that
;; mirrors what upstream's own batch runner has already loaded as a
;; side effect by the time any one file runs.
;;
;; STALENESS WARNING (the failure mode this file is most exposed to):
;; this artifact's :assertions/:deftests totals are a fact about the
;; vendored file SET at the moment this census was run. If a file is
;; later added to, removed from, or edited within
;; tests/clojure-suite/vendor/ and this census is NOT re-run, the
;; committed totals below silently stop matching the actual vendored
;; set -- and because the denominator staying the SAME while mova's
;; numerator changes is exactly what makes the headline percentage
;; look better without mova improving, a stale census is a flattering
;; lie, not just an inaccuracy. The `:vendor-fingerprint` key below
;; (SHA-256 of tests/clojure-suite/MANIFEST.sha256 itself, plus the
;; vendored file count and sorted basenames, computed fresh by
;; tools/oracle-census.sh from the CURRENT vendor/ directory every
;; time this file is regenerated) exists so staleness can be checked
;; CHEAPLY, without re-running this ~44-minute census:
;; tools/generate-compat-report.bb compares this fingerprint against
;; a freshly-computed one on every report run and FAILS its
;; guarantee-check row (with a visible STALE marker next to the
;; headline denominator) on any mismatch. That freshness gate runs on
;; EVERY tools/conformance-report.sh pass; re-running this census
;; itself stays a deliberate, occasional, manual command -- see
;; tools/oracle-census.sh's own module doc for why those two things
;; are deliberately kept separate. An artifact from before this key
;; existed has no `:vendor-fingerprint` at all; the freshness gate
;; renders that as NOT MEASURED (never :pass) and tells the reader to
;; re-run tools/oracle-census.sh.
;;
;; WHAT :load-error MEANS: a file real Clojure itself cannot load even
;; with all of the above gets :status :load-error, :assertions and
;; :deftests nil, and is EXCLUDED from :totals -- but it is still
;; listed below with the verbatim cause-chain reason, and :totals
;; carries both :files-counted and :files-total so the shortfall is
;; visible arithmetic, never a silently shifted denominator. A file
;; whose count MOVED between this census's own two independent runs is
;; flagged :nondeterministic true with both counts in its :note.
;;
;; TAMPERING WARNING: this file must ONLY ever be produced by running
;; tools/oracle-census.sh end to end. Hand-editing any number in here
;; changes the project's headline compatibility percentage without
;; changing anything real about mova or about the suite. If a number
;; here looks wrong, the fix is to fix tools/oracle-census.clj's
;; counting logic (or its classpath/preamble) and regenerate -- never
;; to hand-edit this file.
;;
